{% comment %}
  Oberndoerfer Milano - PRODUCT CARD COLOR SWATCHES (P0.3)
  -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Adds a swatch row under every card in a same-model, different-color
  group, so shoppers can jump straight to another color's product page.
  Every card stays visible and keeps its own price/title - this does
  NOT collapse the grid down to one card per model (an earlier version
  of this snippet did that; the founder asked to see every color card
  again, just with swatches added).

  DISPLAY LAYER ONLY. No product, variant, price, inventory or handle is
  touched. Deleting this snippet just removes the swatch row - the grid
  underneath is completely unaffected either way.

  WHY THIS IS NEEDED
  These products have NO color variant - verified via the Admin API, every
  one reports options: [{name: "Title", values: ["Default Title"]}]. The
  color exists only in the product title, so there is no native swatch UI
  to hang this off of - it has to be built from the title string.

  MATCHING RULE - and the two traps in it
  A title is grouped only when it is exactly "<base> - <color>" AND <base>
  is on the allowlist below. Two reasons the allowlist is not optional:

  1. THE WATCH BOXES. The 2026-08 rename standardised ~25 watch boxes to
     "[Model] - [Variant]", e.g. "8-Place Watchbox - Black Stud". Those
     variants are NOT colors and those products are NOT the same model. A
     generic " - " rule would group them wrongly.
  2. "SAC" vs "SAC ALLIGATOR". Base matching is EXACT, never a prefix.
     "SAC - Black" has base "SAC"; "SAC Alligator - Black" has base
     "SAC Alligator". A prefix match would swallow the alligator range into
     the calf one - different leather, very different price.

  Titles using " in " rather than " - " are correctly left alone, which is
  what keeps "The Mirror Handbag in Ostrich" out of the Mirror Handbag group.

  TWO NAMING PATTERNS, TWO MATCHERS
  Some families write color-first with no separator ("Brown Leather Pouf")
  instead of "<base> - <color>". OB_SUFFIX_GROUPS handles those via an exact
  trailing-words match instead of the hyphen split - same "no
  prefix/substring matching" discipline as OB_GROUPS, just anchored to the
  end of the string instead of a hyphen.

  TO ADD A GROUP: add its exact base title to OB_GROUPS (hyphen pattern) or
  OB_SUFFIX_GROUPS (color-first pattern) below.

  KNOWN EXCEPTIONS:
    - 8-Place Watch Box: titles mostly mix real colors (Green, Red, Grey...)
      with one hardware variant pair (Black Stud vs Black Classic - stud vs
      classic closure, not a color). Founder's call: exclude "Black Stud"
      by exact title via OB_EXCLUDE_TITLES (stays singular, no swatch).
    - Crocodile Wallet: only "- Grey" is ACTIVE; the others are DRAFT.
      Drafts are absent from /products.json too, so the 2+ guard keeps this
      inert until they go live, at which point it turns on by itself.
    - Table Trunk: "Table Trunk" (bare, no color) can't join "Table Trunk -
      Black" because the bare title doesn't match the hyphen split. Inert
      today; fixing the bare title to include its color would turn this on.

  Same PDP-side swatch group lists live in snippets/oberndoerfer-pdp-color-swatches.liquid
  - keep all four lists (2 files x 2 matchers) in sync when adding a group.

  COLOUR DOTS (2026-09-10, owner: "show color instead of mini product images"):
  each dot is now the colour named in the title (OB_COLOURS table, with
  dark/light modifiers), and the average colour of the photograph when the
  name is not in the table. The photograph is only used as a last resort.

  RE-RENDERING: Shopify re-renders these grids on collection filtering and
  paging, and this theme morphs DOM after load, so this runs again on a
  debounced MutationObserver and is fully idempotent - it rebuilds from
  scratch each pass and removes its own previous output first.

  SWATCH ROW DISPLAY CAP (2026-08-15, Miu Miu reference pass): show at most
  4 color dots per card, then a small "+N" for the rest, rather than every
  color's dot in a row.

  SWATCH ROW SPACING (2026-08-16): this row sits inside the same beige text
  panel as title/price (see snippets/product-card-styles.liquid v5). The gap
  is padding-block-start on THIS element rather than margin, so the gap stays
  filled with the row's own beige background and no seam opens between two
  independently-backgrounded elements. !important because a plain declaration
  lost to a theme-base shorthand rule in the homepage product-list context.

  PAGE-WIDE GROUPING (2026-08-21): cards used to be bucketed per GRID
  CONTAINER. Invisible on a collection page (one grid), fatal on the
  homepage, which runs two product-list rows that split every family, so no
  family reached the 2-member threshold and the homepage had no swatches at
  all. Buckets are now keyed on base title across the whole page.

  COMPLETE FAMILIES (2026-08-22): page-wide grouping fixed the homepage but
  left it inconsistent - Leather Watch Box and SAC had dots because two of
  their colors happened to be in the rows, while The Mirror Handbag showed
  none despite existing in five. Founder's call: every grouped card should
  show its WHOLE color range, wherever it appears.

  The family index is therefore built from /products.json (verified on this
  storefront: 129 products, images included, drafts correctly absent) rather
  than from whatever cards happen to share the page. Consequences worth
  knowing:
    - It is fetched ONCE PER SESSION and cached in sessionStorage, reduced to
      {title, handle, img} first so the stored payload is small even though
      the response is not.
    - It is fetched on idle, AFTER a first synchronous DOM-based pass, so
      this never delays anything and never renders less than the old version
      did. The DOM pass is also the fallback if the fetch fails.
    - On the first page of a session the dots can arrive a beat late, so any
      card whose title parses into a group gets a reserved-height placeholder
      row immediately - that is what ob-swatches--pending is for. Every later
      page in the session reads the cache synchronously and never shifts.
    - Colors are sorted alphabetically so the row is stable between pages
      rather than following catalog order.
{% endcomment %}
{% style %}
  .ob-swatches {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 7px;
    margin-block-start: 0;
    padding-block-start: 14px !important;
    min-height: 22px;
  }
  .ob-swatch {
    display: block;
    width: 22px;
    height: 22px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
    background-color: #F0EBE3;
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(24, 18, 12, 0.18);
    outline-offset: 2px;
    transition: box-shadow 0.18s ease;
  }
  .ob-swatch:hover,
  .ob-swatch:focus-visible {
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(24, 18, 12, 0.5);
  }
  .ob-swatch[aria-current='true'] {
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(24, 18, 12, 0.18),
      0 0 0 1px #18120C;
  }
  .ob-swatch-count {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: rgba(24, 18, 12, 0.55);
    margin-inline-start: 3px;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .ob-swatch { transition: none; }
  }
{% endstyle %}

<script>
  (function () {
    /* Exact base titles only. See the snippet comment for why this is an
       allowlist and not a generic " - " rule. */
    var OB_GROUPS = [
      'BAG MODEL 017', 'SAC', 'SAC Alligator', 'The Mirror Handbag',
      'Briefcase', '3-Place Watch Box', '8-Place Watch Box', 'Leather Watch Box',
      'Watch & Jewelry Box', 'Nabuk Leather Jewelry Box', 'Crochet Handbag',
      'Mini Crochet Handbag', 'Leather Sofa', 'Crocodile Wallet', 'Table Trunk'
    ];

    var OB_EXCLUDE_TITLES = ['8-Place Watch Box - Black Stud'];

    var OB_SUFFIX_GROUPS = ['Leather Coaster Set', 'Leather Pouf', 'Leather Tray'];

    var SWATCH_VISIBLE_CAP = 4;
    var CATALOG_KEY = 'obm-catalog-v1';

    var busy = false;
    var familyIndex = null;   // Map base -> [{color, href, img}] once loaded
    var catalogTried = false;

    /* ---- colour of a dot ---- */

    var OB_COLOURS = [
      ['black', '#1a1715'], ['nero', '#1a1715'], ['white', '#f5f4f1'], ['bianco', '#f5f4f1'],
      ['ivory', '#f1ebdd'], ['cream', '#efe6d3'], ['off-white', '#efe9dc'], ['ecru', '#e9dfc9'],
      ['beige', '#d6c4a6'], ['sand', '#d3bf9d'], ['nude', '#d8b8a4'], ['blush', '#e2b8b0'],
      ['taupe', '#8d7c6a'], ['tan', '#c39b6a'], ['camel', '#bd9463'], ['caramel', '#b57a3c'],
      ['cognac', '#9a5a2c'], ['brown', '#6a4a30'], ['marrone', '#6a4a30'], ['chocolate', '#452a1b'],
      ['espresso', '#3c2418'], ['mocha', '#5b4132'], ['bordeaux', '#6a1f2b'], ['burgundy', '#6a1f2b'],
      ['wine', '#6a1f2b'], ['red', '#9c1f1f'], ['rosso', '#9c1f1f'], ['orange', '#d3722a'],
      ['coral', '#e07a6a'], ['pink', '#e3a4bd'], ['rosa', '#e3a4bd'], ['fuchsia', '#c8348a'],
      ['lavender', '#b7a6d2'], ['lilac', '#c3b0da'], ['purple', '#5f3a86'], ['violet', '#5f3a86'],
      ['navy', '#1d2a48'], ['cobalt', '#1f47a8'], ['royal', '#2b4fb5'], ['blue', '#2e4b84'],
      ['blu', '#2e4b84'], ['sky', '#a6c6e5'], ['petrol', '#25596a'], ['teal', '#2c7c86'],
      ['turquoise', '#3fb2b0'], ['mint', '#a7d3c1'], ['sage', '#9aab8f'], ['olive', '#6d6b3d'],
      ['green', '#2f5c3b'], ['verde', '#2f5c3b'], ['forest', '#22412d'], ['emerald', '#1f7a4d'],
      ['khaki', '#8c8354'], ['yellow', '#e4c23a'], ['mustard', '#c99a2e'], ['gold', '#c5a04a'],
      ['silver', '#bdbdbd'], ['grey', '#8b8b8b'], ['gray', '#8b8b8b'], ['charcoal', '#3c3c3c'],
      ['anthracite', '#3c3c3c'], ['graphite', '#4a4a4a'], ['leopard', '#b9975b'],
      ['natural', '#d9cbb3'], ['honey', '#c98f3b'], ['rust', '#a8492a'], ['terracotta', '#b7593a'],
      ['denim', '#4a6491'], ['multicolor', '#b9975b'], ['multicolour', '#b9975b']
    ];

    function namedColour(name) {
      var words = String(name || '').toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z\u00e0-\u00ff\/ -]/g, ' ').split(/[\s\/]+/);
      // two-word names first ("dark blue", "light grey") so the modifier is honoured
      for (var i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
        for (var c = 0; c < OB_COLOURS.length; c++) {
          if (words[i] === OB_COLOURS[c][0]) {
            var hex = OB_COLOURS[c][1];
            if (words[i - 1] === 'dark' || words[i - 1] === 'deep') return shade(hex, -0.35);
            if (words[i - 1] === 'light' || words[i - 1] === 'pale') return shade(hex, 0.55);
            return hex;
          }
        }
      }
      return null;
    }

    function shade(hex, amount) {
      var n = parseInt(hex.slice(1), 16), r = n >> 16, g = (n >> 8) & 255, b = n & 255;
      function mix(v) { return Math.round(amount < 0 ? v * (1 + amount) : v + (255 - v) * amount); }
      return 'rgb(' + mix(r) + ',' + mix(g) + ',' + mix(b) + ')';
    }

    var averageCache = {};

    function averageColour(src, cb) {
      if (!src) { cb(null); return; }
      if (averageCache[src]) { cb(averageCache[src]); return; }
      var img = new Image();
      img.crossOrigin = 'anonymous';
      img.onload = function () {
        try {
          var cv = document.createElement('canvas'), cx = cv.getContext('2d');
          cv.width = 24; cv.height = 24;
          cx.drawImage(img, 0, 0, 24, 24);
          var d = cx.getImageData(0, 0, 24, 24).data, r = 0, g = 0, b = 0, n = 0;
          for (var i = 0; i < d.length; i += 4) {
            // skip the pale studio ground so the dot is the object, not the backdrop
            if (d[i] > 225 && d[i + 1] > 225 && d[i + 2] > 225) continue;
            r += d[i]; g += d[i + 1]; b += d[i + 2]; n++;
          }
          if (!n) { cb(null); return; }
          var out = 'rgb(' + Math.round(r / n) + ',' + Math.round(g / n) + ',' + Math.round(b / n) + ')';
          averageCache[src] = out;
          cb(out);
        } catch (e) { cb(null); }
      };
      img.onerror = function () { cb(null); };
      // a small rendition is enough for an average and keeps the request light
      img.src = src.replace(/(\.[a-z]+)(\?|$)/i, '_120x120$1$2');
    }

    function paintSwatch(el, colourName, imgSrc) {
      var hex = namedColour(colourName);
      if (hex) { el.style.backgroundColor = hex; return; }
      averageColour(imgSrc, function (avg) {
        if (avg) { el.style.backgroundColor = avg; }
        else if (imgSrc) { el.style.backgroundImage = 'url("' + imgSrc + '")'; }
      });
    }

    function titleOf(card) {
      var raw = card.getAttribute('view-event-payload');
      if (raw) {
        try {
          var t = JSON.parse(raw);
          if (t && t.product && t.product.title) return t.product.title;
        } catch (e) { /* fall through */ }
      }
      var link = card.querySelector('a.product-card__link[aria-label]');
      return link ? link.getAttribute('aria-label') : null;
    }

    function imageOf(card) {
      var img = card.querySelector('img');
      if (!img) return null;
      return img.currentSrc || img.getAttribute('src') || null;
    }

    function hrefOf(card) {
      var link = card.querySelector('a[href*="/products/"]');
      return link ? link.getAttribute('href').split('?')[0] : null;
    }

    /* Compare by handle, not by full path - a card's href may carry a locale
       or market prefix that the catalog's /products/<handle> form does not. */
    function handleOf(href) {
      if (!href) return null;
      var parts = href.split('?')[0].split('/');
      return parts[parts.length - 1] || null;
    }

    function splitByHyphen(title) {
      for (var e = 0; e < OB_EXCLUDE_TITLES.length; e++) {
        if (OB_EXCLUDE_TITLES[e].toLowerCase() === title.toLowerCase()) return null;
      }
      var i = title.indexOf(' - ');
      if (i === -1) return null;
      var base = title.slice(0, i).trim();
      var color = title.slice(i + 3).trim();
      if (!base || !color) return null;
      for (var g = 0; g < OB_GROUPS.length; g++) {
        if (OB_GROUPS[g].toLowerCase() === base.toLowerCase()) return {base: base, color: color};
      }
      return null;
    }

    function splitBySuffix(title) {
      for (var s = 0; s < OB_SUFFIX_GROUPS.length; s++) {
        var suffix = OB_SUFFIX_GROUPS[s];
        var marker = ' ' + suffix;
        if (title.length <= marker.length) continue;
        var tail = title.slice(title.length - marker.length);
        if (tail.toLowerCase() !== marker.toLowerCase()) continue;
        var color = title.slice(0, title.length - marker.length).trim();
        if (!color) continue;
        return {base: suffix, color: color};
      }
      return null;
    }

    function split(title) {
      return splitByHyphen(title) || splitBySuffix(title);
    }

    /* ---- catalog: the whole color range, not just what's on this page ---- */

    function indexFrom(list) {
      var m = new Map();
      list.forEach(function (p) {
        var parsed = split(p.title);
        if (!parsed) return;
        var key = parsed.base.toLowerCase();
        if (!m.has(key)) m.set(key, []);
        m.get(key).push({color: parsed.color, href: '/products/' + p.handle, img: p.img});
      });
      m.forEach(function (arr) {
        arr.sort(function (a, b) { return a.color.localeCompare(b.color); });
      });
      return m;
    }

    function loadCatalog() {
      if (catalogTried) return;
      catalogTried = true;

      try {
        var cached = sessionStorage.getItem(CATALOG_KEY);
        if (cached) {
          familyIndex = indexFrom(JSON.parse(cached));
          run();
          return;
        }
      } catch (e) { /* unreadable cache: just fetch */ }

      var all = [];
      function page(n) {
        fetch('/products.json?limit=250&page=' + n, {credentials: 'same-origin'})
          .then(function (r) { return r.ok ? r.json() : null; })
          .then(function (j) {
            var got = (j && j.products) || [];
            for (var i = 0; i < got.length; i++) {
              all.push({
                title: got[i].title,
                handle: got[i].handle,
                img: (got[i].images && got[i].images[0] && got[i].images[0].src) || null
              });
            }
            // keep paging while a full page comes back; the cap is a guard
            // against ever looping on an endpoint that misbehaves
            if (got.length === 250 && n < 8) { page(n + 1); return; }
            done();
          })
          .catch(done);
      }
      function done() {
        if (!all.length) { run(); return; }   // fetch failed: DOM pass stands
        try { sessionStorage.setItem(CATALOG_KEY, JSON.stringify(all)); } catch (e) {}
        familyIndex = indexFrom(all);
        run();
      }
      page(1);
    }

    /* ---- render ---- */

    function run() {
      if (busy) return;
      busy = true;
      try {
        var cards = document.querySelectorAll('product-card');
        if (!cards.length) return;

        document.querySelectorAll('.ob-swatches').forEach(function (n) { n.remove(); });

        var byBase = new Map();
        var anyGroupable = false;
        cards.forEach(function (card) {
          var title = titleOf(card);
          if (!title) return;
          var parsed = split(title);
          if (!parsed) return;
          anyGroupable = true;
          var key = parsed.base.toLowerCase();
          if (!byBase.has(key)) byBase.set(key, []);
          byBase.get(key).push({card: card, color: parsed.color,
                                href: hrefOf(card), img: imageOf(card)});
        });

        byBase.forEach(function (members, key) {
          // The full range when the catalog is loaded; otherwise whatever is
          // on this page, de-duplicated by product so a model appearing in
          // two rows contributes one dot and cannot group with itself.
          var palette;
          if (familyIndex && familyIndex.has(key)) {
            palette = familyIndex.get(key);
          } else {
            palette = [];
            var seen = {};
            members.forEach(function (m) {
              if (!m.href || seen[m.href]) return;
              seen[m.href] = true;
              palette.push(m);
            });
          }

          if (palette.length < 2) {
            // Nothing to show. If the catalog is still in flight this card
            // might still gain a row, so hold its height until we know.
            if (!familyIndex) {
              members.forEach(function (self) {
                var hold = document.createElement('div');
                hold.className = 'ob-swatches ob-swatches--pending';
                hold.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
                (self.card.querySelector('.product-card__content') || self.card).appendChild(hold);
              });
            }
            return;
          }

          members.forEach(function (self) {
            var row = document.createElement('div');
            row.className = 'ob-swatches';
            row.setAttribute('role', 'group');
            row.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Available colors');

            var selfHandle = handleOf(self.href);
            var selfEntry = null;
            for (var i = 0; i < palette.length; i++) {
              if (handleOf(palette[i].href) === selfHandle) { selfEntry = palette[i]; break; }
            }

            // Always keep THIS card's own color visible and marked current,
            // even if it would fall past the cap, so a shopper never loses
            // track of which color they are looking at.
            var visible = palette.slice(0, SWATCH_VISIBLE_CAP);
            if (selfEntry && visible.indexOf(selfEntry) === -1) {
              visible = visible.slice(0, Math.max(SWATCH_VISIBLE_CAP - 1, 0)).concat([selfEntry]);
            }

            visible.forEach(function (m) {
              if (!m.href) return;
              var a = document.createElement('a');
              a.className = 'ob-swatch';
              a.setAttribute('href', m.href);
              a.setAttribute('title', m.color);
              a.setAttribute('aria-label', m.color);
              if (selfEntry && m === selfEntry) a.setAttribute('aria-current', 'true');
              // the dot shows the colour itself (owner, 10 Sept: "show color instead of
              // mini product images"): a named colour from the title, or the average
              // colour of the photograph when the name is not in the table
              var src = (selfEntry && m === selfEntry && self.img) ? self.img : m.img;
              paintSwatch(a, m.color, src);
              row.appendChild(a);
            });

            var remaining = palette.length - visible.length;
            if (remaining > 0) {
              var count = document.createElement('span');
              count.className = 'ob-swatch-count';
              count.textContent = '+' + remaining;
              row.appendChild(count);
            }

            (self.card.querySelector('.product-card__content') || self.card).appendChild(row);
          });
        });

        // Only go to the network if this page actually has something to
        // complete, and only when the browser is otherwise idle.
        if (anyGroupable && !familyIndex && !catalogTried) {
          if (window.requestIdleCallback) requestIdleCallback(loadCatalog, {timeout: 2000});
          else setTimeout(loadCatalog, 400);
        }
      } finally {
        busy = false;
      }
    }

    function debounced() {
      clearTimeout(debounced._t);
      debounced._t = setTimeout(run, 120);
    }

    if (document.readyState !== 'loading') run();
    else document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', run);
    document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', debounced);

    var mo = new MutationObserver(function (records) {
      for (var i = 0; i < records.length; i++) {
        var t = records[i].target;
        if (t && t.closest && t.closest('.ob-swatches')) continue; // our own output
        return debounced();
      }
    });
    if (document.body) mo.observe(document.body, {childList: true, subtree: true});
  })();
</script>
